claim.claim-text:
a fluid source (10);
a flow diverter (30) fluidly connected to the fluid source (10), wherein the flow diverter (30) is configured to remove a portion of the fluid from the fluid source (10);
an oxygenator (40) fluidly connected to the fluid source (10), wherein the oxygenator (40) is configured to oxygenate fluid from the fluid source (10);
a bypass line (100) or a non-gas-exchange shunt channel through the oxygenator (40) fluidly connected to the flow diverter (30); wherein the fluid from the flow diverter (30) passes into the oxygenator (40) and into the bypass line (100) or the non-gas-exchange shunt channel through the oxygenator (40);
a filter (50) in fluid communication with the bypass line (100), wherein the filter (50) is configured to remove gaseous microemboli having a diameter greater than a pore size of the filter (50);
an outlet (80) fluidly connected to the oxygenator (40) and the bypass line (100) or the non-gas-exchange shunt channel.

shunting fluid through a non-gas-exchange shunt channel which is a filtered shunt flow channel within the oxygenator (40);
introducing a fluid to the oxygenator (40);
oxygenating the fluid passing through the oxygenator (40).
